  "worked_solution": "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2} & =13{v}_{1}-7{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2} \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7({v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7(0) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=T(13{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(13{v}_{1}) & =13T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =13[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].$",
